  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given two numbers lll and rrr, count the number of non-negative integers xxx such that there exists a pair of integers (a,b)(a, b)(a,b) that satisfy the following requirements:\n\n\nx=a⊕b=a+bx = a \\oplus b = a + bx=a⊕b=a+b\nl≤a≤b≤rl \\leq a \\leq b \\leq rl≤a≤b≤r.\nHere ⊕\\oplus⊕ refers to the bitwise operation of XOR.\n\nNote: You should output the number of xxx. Not the number of pairs (a,b)(a, b)(a,b).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The test cases follow.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input consisting of two numbers lll and rrr.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the number of non-negative integers xxx that satisfy the requirements.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "0≤l≤r≤10180 \\leq l \\leq r \\leq 10^{18}0≤l≤r≤1018",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (5 points):** 1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10, 0≤l,r≤1000 \\leq l, r \\leq 1000≤l,r≤100.",
      "**Subtask 2 (7 points):** 1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105, l=0l = 0l=0, r=2k−1≤1018r = 2^{k} - 1 \\leq 10^{18}r=2k−1≤1018",
      "**Subtask 3 (13 points):** 1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105, l=0,r≤1018l = 0, r \\leq 10^{18}l=0,r≤1018",
      "**Subtask 4 (20 points):** 1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10, 0≤l,r≤1050 \\leq l, r \\leq 10^{5}0≤l,r≤105.",
      "**Subtask 5 (55 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2 2\n1 4",
        "output": "0\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn the first case, the only possibility is a=2a=2a=2 and b=2b=2b=2. But a+b=4a+b = 4a+b=4 and a⊕b=0a \\oplus b = 0a⊕b=0. Hence, there is no xxx which satisfies the requirements, and so the answer is 000.\nIn the second case, we can write\n\n3=1+2=1⊕23 = 1 + 2 = 1 \\oplus 2 3=1+2=1⊕2\n5=1+4=1⊕45 = 1 + 4 = 1 \\oplus 45=1+4=1⊕4\n6=2+4=2⊕46 = 2 + 4 = 2 \\oplus 46=2+4=2⊕4\n7=3+4=3⊕47 = 3 + 4 = 3 \\oplus 47=3+4=3⊕4\n\n\n\nIt can be shown that these are the non-negative integers which satisfy the requirements. Hence the total number of xxx which satisfies the requirements is 444."
      }
    ]
  },
